<main class="container page-container k-screen-set k-screen-set-public">
    <section class="page-header-center k-screen-header">
        <span class="badge-pill eyebrow">The Orchestration Model</span>
        <h1 class="page-title">How Kurukoo Works</h1>
        <p class="page-desc">Tell Kurukoo what you need. Kurukoo figures out who or what can fulfil it.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="k-context-band" aria-label="Request lifecycle context"><div class="k-context-mark" aria-hidden="true">K</div><div><strong>One request, visible boundaries</strong><span>Conversation, options, quote, payment and fulfilment each retain their own evidence state. Kurukoo shows only the next supported action and keeps the original context connected.</span></div><a href="/chat?prompt=Help%20me%20start%20a%20request">Continue in Chat</a></section>

    <section class="how-process-summary k-screen-grid" aria-label="Kurukoo request flow"><div class="step-card k-screen-card"><div class="step-number">01</div><h3>Start with a need</h3><p>Say what you want in your own words. You do not need to know which service, provider or category should handle it.</p></div><div class="step-card k-screen-card"><div class="step-number">02</div><h3>Kurukoo organises it</h3><p>The conversation captures the requirements, context and next step without making you repeat the request.</p></div><div class="step-card k-screen-card"><div class="step-number">03</div><h3>See the useful step</h3><p>Only supported, known states are shown as known. Unavailable fulfilment paths remain clearly bounded.</p></div></section>

    <div class="how-it-works-grid">
        <div class="step-card k-screen-card"><div class="step-number">01</div><h3>Tell Kurukoo what you need</h3><p>Start in Web Chat and describe the need in plain language. Kurukoo keeps the request in context without asking you to repeat it after a required sign-in step.</p></div>
        <div class="step-card k-screen-card"><div class="step-number">02</div><h3>Kurukoo assesses the request</h3><p>Kurukoo identifies the relevant request path and checks whether the underlying skill, provider data, or connector support is available.</p></div>
        <div class="step-card k-screen-card"><div class="step-number">03</div><h3>Review a supported next step</h3><p>A provider, quote, or offer is presented only when its underlying data and authorization boundary are available.</p></div>
        <div class="step-card k-screen-card"><div class="step-number">04</div><h3>Confirm eligible actions</h3><p>Protected actions request identity when necessary. Payment, escrow, delivery, and fulfilment steps appear only where their verified integrations are available.</p></div>
    </div>

    <section class="request-boundaries-panel k-screen-panel" aria-labelledby="request-boundaries-title"><div class="section-heading section-heading--left"><span class="eyebrow">Request states</span><h2 id="request-boundaries-title">One request, visible boundaries.</h2><p>Kurukoo keeps the useful distinction between a conversation, a supported option, a confirmed quote, payment, escrow, and fulfilment.</p></div><div class="how-it-works-grid request-boundaries-grid"><div class="step-card k-screen-card"><h3>Capture</h3><p>Conversation collects the request details.</p></div><div class="step-card k-screen-card"><h3>Coordinate</h3><p>Eligible options are considered against real availability.</p></div><div class="step-card k-screen-card"><h3>Confirm</h3><p>A quote or next step is shown only when its state is known.</p></div><div class="step-card k-screen-card"><h3>Fulfil</h3><p>Any coordination follows the same Economic Request lifecycle.</p></div></div></section>

    <section class="how-it-works-cta"><div class="cta-box k-screen-panel"><h2>Ready to get started?</h2><p>Start a conversation and Kurukoo will show the supported path for the request.</p><a href="/chat" class="btn btn-primary">Start chatting</a></div></section>
</main>

